  "_bannerSlots_note": "Auto-latest roster: sync-models.js resolves each slot to the NEWEST FLAGSHIP catalog model whose id starts with `match` and contains none of `exclude`, by `created` timestamp. Excludes must drop sub-flagship tiers so 'newest' means newest flagship (e.g. Claude excludes `sonnet`/`haiku` \u2192 resolves the premium `claude-fable-*`, not the newer mid-tier Sonnet). `pin` forces an exact id; optional `expect` substring warns when the resolved id lacks it (catalog lags a known launch). The provider set + excludes are editorial \u2014 tune at the desk; the resolution mechanism is what's tested. Resolved slots are written to `bannerModels` (front-page banner ONLY) \u2014 they do NOT enter `models`, so the markets table + Cost-of-Intelligence index stay on the curated trackedModels. Each sync also prints a Banner Roster report and writes data/banner-roster.json (the easy check). trackedModels/evals are the curated current frontier \u2014 refresh them at the desk to match the auto-resolved banner; bannerKeys is the backward-compat banner fallback.",
